; Rekindled, not freed: Artemis, the huntress and the moon, the first god of the far shore (.ai/second-half.md 3.2-3.4;
; F2). Named in the legend of Laelaps - she gave the hound to Procris - and rekindled when the White Downs' warden falls
; (UnlockCatalog.FromGod, the seat deed AchievementDefinitions.SeatClear writes for stage_14). Hidden from the character
; select until her seat opens, then a silhouette with her held line. Her sheet is tools/art/player_artemis.py.
;
; She opens on Sagittarius, made, at level 1 of its own table (ComboDefinition.StartsFusedFor), as the Dark Wizard
; opens on The Taking: a bow and the stars as archers. Her Apotheosis on it is The Hunter's Moon (hunt). Her passive is
; Far-Shooting: every spell finds its target and flies to it 15% farther (SpellData.ReachScale) - an axis no wizard
; owns, and none of it damage. Lighter than the wizards and quicker on her feet: 0.90 health, 1.08 speed, the first
; guesses of the doc's table - and walking is half of what her spell asks.
